evan: Heads-up — Nimbus wants a short POC next week. They need streaming + function/tool calls + strictly structured JSON output for downstream ingestion. Also asked for a rough pricing impact if we enable streaming + high QPS (estimated 200 rps).

leah: Got it. Main asks: 1) streaming SDK sample, 2) structured output schema enforcement, 3) pricing delta for 200rps sustained, 4) security questionnaire answers (SAML, KMS).

mike: I can do SDK sample and perf numbers. For streaming at 200 rps we should size for batching and KV cache hitrates. Estimate: with 1.3 tokens/resp avg and 1.2x overhead for tool calls, roughly $X/day — will run numbers after I know typical token sizes.

ev an: @mike (typo) — can you draft a quick JS streaming snippet they can run in the POC? Keep it minimal. Also include how to surface function/tool call events (they want to route tool outputs to internal webhook).

mike: sure. quick example (JS, node):

```js
// minimal streaming + function call handler (node)
const Redwood = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });

(async () => {
  const stream = await client.stream({
    model: 'redwood-large-v1',
    input: 'Summarize this invoice and return JSON schema',
    tool_hooks: {
      onToolCall: (call) => {
        // call = { name, args, id }
        fetch('https://internal-hook/nimbus', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(call) });
      }
    }
  });

  for await (const chunk of stream) {
    process.stdout.write(chunk.text);
  }
})();
```

mike: For structured output we recommend the `format: json-schema` flag and a schema attached to the request so model enforces keys and types. If a strict schema is required, enable `strict_output` in the request and we will surface a non-2xx containing the model's last-best attempt + diagnostics.

ada: For the security questionnaire: SAML SSO is supported on Dedicated/Private, KMS integrations are available (AWS KMS + GCP CMEK), and we can provide SOC2/ISO artifacts. If they need on-prem air-gapped, Private deployment plan required. I'll pull the standard answers and attach the doc.

leah: Nimbus also asked about rate-limit/backoff behavior for streaming connectors. What happens if they send bursts > 200 rps?

mike: Short answer: adaptive throttling + queued batching. If burst exceeds provisioned Dedicated capacity we fallback to lower-tier model variant (configurable) or return 429 depending on rollout policy. For POC recommend enabling short burst capacity and graceful-fallback to `redwood-small-v1` to preserve availability.

presales-bot: Deploy check: created temp dedicated pool for nimbus-poc (3x A100 equiv) valid 7 days. Links: https://console.redwood/dedicated/pools/nimbus-poc

leah: Nice. @evan can you confirm POC success criteria so we can size pricing correctly? They want <150ms p50 latency for 512-token responses, structured JSON 99.9% conformity, and webhook delivery <500ms end-to-end.

ev an: Confirmed. Also they asked for an itemized cost delta: streaming + tool calls + reserved burst. @mike can you give 3 scenarios (low/med/high) with daily and monthly totals?

mike: Will do — I need a token distribution. If they don't have one, I'll run synthetic with avg 512 tokens per response, 200 rps sustained, 8h/day traffic window. I'll post numbers in ~2 hours.

ada: I'll attach the security Q&A and the KMS config notes to the thread when ready. Legal-bot: we may need an NDA amendment for remote webhook ingestion — can you flag?

legal-bot: Flag noted. Please add the Nimbus legal contact and I'll loop in contracts for an amendment.

leah: Next steps: 1) @mike posts cost scenarios, 2) @mike drops the lightweight SDK sample + curl webhook example, 3) @ada attaches security Q&A and KMS config, 4) evan to schedule kickoff and send Nimbus contact to legal.

ev an: Thanks team — scheduling kickoff for Tue 10am PT. I'll send calendar invites and the Nimbus contact now. :thumbsup:

mike: Posted numbers in a follow-up thread (see link) and included a small load-test script they can run locally.

leah: Great. closing this thread after kickoff; keep updates here for auditability. :white_check_mark:
